CAT = "aesiraReports"; SEG = "REP"
Q = [
("When should a guard write up an incident in the notebook or log?",
 "As soon as possible", ["At the end of the week", "Only if the police ask", "Only when a supervisor asks"],
 "Notes made straight after an event are the most accurate and carry more weight as evidence. Memory fades quickly."),
("A guard's incident report says what happened but not where or when. What is the main problem?",
 "Key facts are missing", ["It has no opinions in it", "It names the people involved", "It was written in pen, not typed"],
 "A report must cover who, what, where, when and how. Without place and time it cannot be matched to CCTV or witness accounts."),
("A guard makes a mistake in the pocket notebook. How should it be corrected?",
 "One line through, initialled", ["Tear out the whole page", "Cover it with correction fluid", "Scribble it out fully"],
 "A single line keeps the original readable and shows nothing was hidden. Removed pages or blotted entries raise doubts about the whole record."),
("Which entry belongs in an incident report?",
 "\"The man pushed the door twice\"", ["\"He looked like a thief to me\"", "\"I think he was drunk at the time\"", "\"He was clearly guilty\""],
 "Reports record what was seen and heard, not opinions or guesses. The reader, or a court, draws the conclusions."),
("Times in a guard's report should be written:",
 "Exactly, as the time it happened", ["Rounded to the nearest day", "Only as 'morning' or 'night'", "As the time the report was typed"],
 "Exact times (for example 23:42) let the account be matched to CCTV, access logs and witness statements."),
("When describing a suspect, which detail is most useful because it is hard to change quickly?",
 "Height and build", ["Colour of the cap", "A carried shopping bag", "Sunglasses"],
 "Clothing and accessories can be removed in seconds. Height, build, scars and gait stay the same and help police identify a person."),
("Which description of a vehicle is most useful to the police?",
 "Plate, make, colour, emirate", ["\"A fast white car, quite new\"", "\"An expensive-looking car\"", "\"A car like my brother's\""],
 "The plate number with the issuing emirate, make, model and colour lets police trace a vehicle. Vague impressions do not."),
("A theft has happened in a shop and the area is now quiet. The guard's role at the scene is to:",
 "Keep people out of the area", ["Tidy up the broken glass", "Gather up the dropped items", "Ask shoppers to help search"],
 "Preserving the scene protects fingerprints, footprints and other evidence. Cleaning or touching items can destroy it."),
("A guard must enter a crime scene to give first aid to an injured person. What else should the guard do?",
 "Note what was moved and why", ["Clean the area afterwards", "Move everything to the side", "Not tell the police"],
 "Saving life comes first. The guard then tells the police exactly what was touched or moved so evidence can be interpreted correctly."),
("A guard finds a mobile phone on a mall bench. What is the correct procedure?",
 "Log it and hand it in", ["Keep it if no one asks", "Give it to the nearest shopper", "Check its messages for the owner"],
 "Found property is recorded (time, place, description) and handed over under the site procedure, for example to lost and found or the police."),
("Why is CCTV footage of an incident saved promptly?",
 "Old footage gets overwritten", ["It looks clearer when it is fresh", "Police cannot copy it later", "It needs editing first"],
 "Most recorders overwrite after a set number of days. Saving the clip quickly, unedited, keeps the evidence for the police."),
("A guard saves CCTV footage of a fight for the police. Which action could damage it as evidence?",
 "Editing or cutting the clip", ["Noting the camera number", "Recording the time saved", "Keeping it in a secure place"],
 "Evidence must be original and unaltered. Editing raises questions about what was removed. Noting who saved it and when keeps the chain of custody."),
("What is meant by the 'chain of custody' for evidence?",
 "A record of who held it and when", ["The set of handcuffs used in arrests", "The order of shift changes", "The client's billing record"],
 "It shows every person who handled the evidence from collection to court, proving it was not tampered with."),
("A witness to an incident wants to leave. The guard should ask for:",
 "Name and contact details", ["Their passport to keep", "Their bank card details", "Their phone to check photos"],
 "Contact details let police follow up. A guard has no power to hold a witness or take their documents or phone."),
("Two witnesses give different accounts of a fight. How should the guard record them?",
 "Record each account as given", ["Record only the more likely one", "Merge them into one story", "Record neither of the two"],
 "Each witness's account is noted as given. Deciding who is right is for the police and investigators."),
("Which writing style suits a security report?",
 "Plain words, in time order", ["Slang and abbreviations", "Long emotional sentences", "Guesses about people's motives"],
 "Reports are read by supervisors, clients, police and courts. Clear words in time order make them easy to follow and hard to dispute."),
("A guard forgets to record an incident and remembers it next shift. What should the guard do?",
 "Write it now, marked as late", ["Back-date it to look on time", "Skip it to avoid any trouble", "Ask a colleague to sign it"],
 "A late entry is made honestly, showing when it was written. Back-dating or false signatures are dishonest and can be an offence."),
("What is the purpose of the daily occurrence book (log book) at a post?",
 "A timed record of the shift", ["A list of guards' salaries", "A book for visitors' comments", "A diary of personal notes"],
 "The occurrence book records patrols, incidents, handovers and calls in time order, giving the next shift and managers a full picture."),
("A guard is asked by a client to remove an entry about a guard error from the log. The guard should:",
 "Refuse and keep the record", ["Remove it to please the client", "Rewrite the whole page", "Tear the page out quietly"],
 "Logs must be true and complete. Removing entries is falsifying records and breaches the guard's integrity duty."),
("When describing a person, the 'top to toe' method means:",
 "Head first, working down", ["Describing only the shoes", "Starting with what they carried", "Listing only clothing colours"],
 "Working from head to feet makes sure nothing is missed: hair, face, build, clothing, footwear and distinguishing marks."),
("A guard hears a loud bang from a car park and then sees a car speed away. In the report the guard should write:",
 "The bang, then the car leaving", ["That a gun was fired at someone", "That the driver was a criminal", "Only the car's speed"],
 "The guard reports the facts in order (a loud bang, then a car leaving). Calling it a gunshot is a conclusion the guard cannot confirm."),
("A guard's notebook is needed by the police in an investigation. This is a reason to:",
 "Keep entries clear and dated", ["Write every note in pencil", "Leave blank pages between notes", "Write the notes in a code"],
 "A notebook may become evidence. Dated, legible entries in ink with no gaps show it was kept honestly at the time."),
("A guard handles a suspicious bag for a few seconds before seeing it is a threat. In the report the guard should:",
 "Say honestly they touched it", ["Leave the contact out of it", "Say a colleague touched it", "Wipe the bag clean first"],
 "Investigators need to know who touched what, to explain prints or DNA. Honest reporting protects the guard and the inquiry."),
("Who is likely to read a guard's incident report?",
 "Managers, police and courts", ["Only the guard who wrote it", "Only SIRA licensing staff", "Only the cleaning team"],
 "Reports go to managers and clients and may be passed to police or used in court, so they must stand up to close reading."),
("A guard sees a staff member slip a watch into a bag at a store exit. Which note is best?",
 "\"21:15, staff put watch in bag\"", ["\"Staff member stole a watch\"", "\"Suspicious behaviour seen\"", "\"That staff member is a thief\""],
 "The best note is factual and timed. Whether it was theft is decided later; 'suspicious behaviour' is too vague to help."),
("Why should a guard avoid discussing an incident on social media?",
 "It can breach privacy", ["It makes reports shorter", "Police prefer public posts", "It is a SIRA reporting channel"],
 "Posting details can breach confidentiality and UAE privacy law, alert suspects and damage an investigation."),
("A guard notices a car parked in the same spot outside a bank for three days with someone inside watching. The guard should:",
 "Note the details and report it", ["Knock and demand ID", "Let the tyres down", "Photograph the driver for social media"],
 "Repeated watching may be planning for a crime. Recording the plate, times and description and reporting it lets the police assess it."),
("When giving information to a 999 operator, the guard should first state:",
 "The exact location", ["The guard's salary grade", "The company's history", "The weather"],
 "The operator needs to know where to send help first. Building name, area and nearest landmark come before other details."),
]
